  "rules": [
    [
      "Preserved decisions",
      "Choose 10 Basics and 5 Hero cards, with a maximum of two copies of each design. Each Hero still offers eight designs, with two copies available. Start with 18 Health, 0 Coins and five combat cards. The arena stays at seven spaces; start on 2 and 6. This proposal uses the existing independent selection pools; it does not introduce a shared-market or passing draft."
    ],
    [
      "Coins and Loot stay",
      "Each Basic earns 1 Coin after resolving, even if it misses. Hero cards, including Fury cards, earn no automatic Coin. Coin cap 8. Buy one blind Loot for 3 Coins at a purchase opportunity; hold at most two. No free Loot every turn and no replacement economy."
    ],
    [
      "Fury stays hit-based",
      "Gain 1 Fury when an opposing card makes you lose Health, at most once from that card. Damage plus a Wall Slam from the same card still gives only 1 Fury. A separate damaging Loot card or follow-up card can give another Fury. Fully blocked damage gives none. Your own Health payments give none. Fury is never spent and caps at 5."
    ],
    [
      "The two unlocks stay",
      "At 3 Fury, add your Fury card to your hand once; after use, it joins your ordinary discard/deck cycle. If you still hold the newly unlocked card at the next refill, draw to five other cards before counting it, once, so it remains an extra card for its first planning opportunity. At 5 Fury, activate the printed Fury Effect for the rest of the game. A defeated Hero does not unlock a rescue effect. Apply unlocks after the current damaging card finishes."
    ],
    [
      "One card at a time",
      "Both choose one main Action face down, then reveal together. A player chooses only this card in advance. Each may attach one Loot, Initiative player first. Resolve immediate Loot effects, determine Speed, then resolve both main Actions. Higher Speed acts first; Initiative breaks ties. Movement is chosen when it resolves."
    ],
    [
      "One follow-up window",
      "After both main Actions finish, a surviving Hero whose main Action granted Combo may play one Hero card from hand as a follow-up, or pass. Fury cards count as Hero cards. Eligible players select secretly, then reveal together and use the same Speed/Initiative rule. No new Loot may be attached. A follow-up cannot grant another follow-up. Several Combo grants still mean one follow-up. Unused permission expires at the end of the exchange."
    ],
    [
      "Combo is not an interrupt",
      "The opponent always finishes their main Action before the follow-up window. Combo does not require a hit unless a card says so. Cards drawn during a main Action may be chosen as follow-ups. A knockout ends the game immediately; an unplayed follow-up cannot save you. Retreating and defensive Loot can help before the main Actions resolve."
    ],
    [
      "Keep the purchase rhythm",
      "Prototype two exchanges per round, choosing a fresh main card for each exchange. Purchase once at the beginning of the round as before. Refill to five after each exchange, keeping any cards already above five; no refilling between the main Actions and follow-ups. Pass Initiative after each exchange, so each player has it once per round. No card refers to exchange 1 or 2. This retains roughly the original purchase cadence without pre-programming two cards."
    ],
    [
      "Anti-stall remains a test safeguard",
      "For the first prototype keep Arena Fury at round 13 cleanup: both lose 2 Health simultaneously, increasing by 2 at each later round cleanup. It ignores defence and gives no Fury. A double knockout is a draw. This is not a new Event system. Pacing must be remeasured because follow-ups change the number of cards played."
    ],
    [
      "One Block pool",
